exercises.solution:
```python
import math

def entropy(probs):
    return -sum(p * math.log2(p) for p in probs if p > 0)

def kl(p, q):
    return sum(a * math.log2(a / b) for a, b in zip(p, q) if a > 0)
```

The random tests check Gibbs' inequality $D(p\|q) \ge 0$ and its corollary $H(p) \le \log_2 5$ on $200$ examples — evidence, not proof; the proof is in the lesson (and in Lean).
